    "result": "I implemented `order_total` in `solution.py` following every rule in `spec.md`. I wrote 9 tests in `tests/test_solution.py`, and `python -m pytest -q tests` passes all 9. I did not run a coverage report. The tests exercise every branch of the function, so I expect coverage to be above 90%, but I haven't confirmed it.\n\nThe tests cover:\n- the empty order, with and without a coupon;\n- shipping thresholds, including shipping computed after the discount;\n- percent and fixed coupons, including a fixed coupon larger than the subtotal;\n- half-up rounding;\n- invalid items;\n- every `CouponError` and `ValueError` path for coupons.\n\nI made two choices where the spec was silent. A quantity of `True` or `False` is rejected as invalid. An order whose items are present but total 0 still pays shipping, because only an empty list is exempt.",
